{
  "statement": "Trustworthiness is crucial for the bookkeeping system, ensuring data protection, access control, and integrity. TRU-01 mandates encryption for financial transactions, safeguarding data during transmission and storage. TRU-02 establishes role-based access control to restrict user permissions, enhancing security. TRU-03 ensures an immutable audit trail, which is vital for accountability. TRU-04 prevents unauthorized data entry through validation. TRU-05 supports two-factor authentication, strengthening user access security. TRU-06 logs user access and modifications, while TRU-07 restricts data access to relevant accounts. However, I see potential conflicts with EFF-04 and SAF-03 due to the performance impact of maintaining detailed logs and ensuring compliance.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["EFF-04"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "The need for quick report generation (EFF-04) may conflict with maintaining a detailed audit trail required by TRU-03."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["SAF-03"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "The emphasis on maintaining an immutable audit trail (TRU-03) could impact performance due to the required detailed logging outlined in SAF-03."
    }
  ],
